From 02e38c5fa2d7a7bc1fee0cf4cc84b73733430bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:51:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: one implementation of the entry points for
 all backends

The generated functions now call the generic functions of
`MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/Integrate.hxx` (`integrateBatch`,
`executeInitializeFunctionOnBatch`, `executePostProcessingOnBatch` and
`rotateBatch`) with the primitive of the backend, built by its public
`makeApply` function. The four entry points written for each backend are
removed.

- `AbstractBackend::getApply` returns the expression building the
  primitive. The default `writeCall` appends it to the arguments.
- The SYCL backend keeps its own entry points, which transfer the fields
  before calling the generic functions. They share one helper
  (`callWithDeviceData`). The copies are now synchronous and the transfer
  policy is handled by `DeviceCopies`.
- The function objects applied at one point share their data
  (`PointFunctionData`). The choice between direct accesses and local
  copies is made by one function (`dispatchStorage`).
- `gather` and `scatter` call `gatherValues` and `scatterValues`.
- The three integration strategies of finite strain behaviours are one
  class template, parametrised by the formulation.
---
